title: 'cumulus-collator: emit the scheduling-signal tail as validate_block does'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The collator skips a collation whose scheduling UMP signals some runtime's `validate_block`
    would reject or rewrite: a signal that does not decode exactly, or two different signals of one
    variant. Other signals pass through in the blocks' order with identical repeats kept once,
    which every runtime's `validate_block` reproduces, including runtimes from before it
    re-encoded the tail and that emit their signals in every block of a PoV.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-collator
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: minor
